A:$ \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115843 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115248 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6f890b-fab1-51f1-9ac7-b680553c835a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Matrix Product That's Equivalent To a Sequence of Row Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ef54140-2672-5265-b691-9d3fb2cd1f4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327064} {:answer/id #uuid "2e06b7d4-773b-593e-9815-139447a16f89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327347} {:answer/id #uuid "471c510b-7774-5214-a739-2e988dc25336" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327553} {:answer/id #uuid "b4b73e26-2fde-583d-8e80-fea1bc66c31f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328505} {:answer/id #uuid "c3da354f-f4b4-5dbb-a0bf-56621d302948" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328646}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "471c510b-7774-5214-a739-2e988dc25336" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327553} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9822533-fbcf-5b20-a3af-01eaee0b139a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329541}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "fd3b5a32-f5f9-54aa-b2af-a91ccc349130" :question/math-academy-id "q-42767" :question/problem "Suppose that the following elementary row operations, in the given order, are to be applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A:$\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:=-2{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1}\n$$\n\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the two given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:=-2{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:=-2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second elementary row operation is ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The third elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$\n\nFinally, to apply the third elementary row operation to ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{3}$ on the left and get ${E}_{3}{E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552440 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115247 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "94c2cd65-810b-52ad-a20d-7b5a0a9eaf2b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Matrix Product That's Equivalent To a Given Row Operation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15d6e35e-81a7-51c8-a7cc-f32f8bec0ceb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551711} {:answer/id #uuid "8f86283f-18b3-551e-a40d-cf34a8f4063d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552016} {:answer/id #uuid "b16f32c5-9c6a-55cb-ad66-50b0738320e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552093} {:answer/id #uuid "c9ef215c-9e2e-51a9-8bc6-e53e4bf54b39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552147} {:answer/id #uuid "cc0a04ef-d28b-50c5-a529-054c7b32dde9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552152}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f86283f-18b3-551e-a40d-cf34a8f4063d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552016} :answer-field/id #uuid "8fc02b48-7c0b-5dca-8522-1bed2f8f771b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552338}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "59ac31ae-d95c-5ade-b172-6fbd672350bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-42811" :question/problem "Suppose we are applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:=\\frac{3}{2}{R}_{2}\\,$ to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A.$ Find the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "We need to find an elementary matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:=\\frac{3}{2}{R}_{2}$  to $A.$ \n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{3}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329687 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115246 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f0f47800-98b3-512e-af20-1899e6b0c86d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Row Operation That's Equivalent To Left Multiplication by an Elementary Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "026c7004-8494-5ac7-b146-bd83da70b93c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:=-4{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326961} {:answer/id #uuid "2dc553fa-6372-54a1-80cf-6f418a317470" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327342} {:answer/id #uuid "59e0fb20-5f68-5538-924e-54424e3a674e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=-4{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327724} {:answer/id #uuid "80510d9c-0bde-550b-9d76-7c48e94ee945" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-4){R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328040} {:answer/id #uuid "b6ea519f-6c58-5a67-b687-351fe81c79a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:=4{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328524}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "026c7004-8494-5ac7-b146-bd83da70b93c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:=-4{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326961} :answer-field/id #uuid "a89561ad-ace0-5390-80f1-311ee4c1f3e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329476}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e243a04a-20ca-53ba-bf29-0d9f8f727a6a" :question/math-academy-id "q-42813" :question/problem "Let $E=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find the row operation that, when applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ gives the result of the product $EA.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $E$ is obtained by multiplying the first row of the identity matrix  by $-4$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the row operation ${R}_{1}:=-4{R}_{1}$ to $A.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552450 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115246 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f0f47800-98b3-512e-af20-1899e6b0c86d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Row Operation That's Equivalent To Left Multiplication by an Elementary Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08830d78-3dad-5449-8109-359dc60bc730" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+6{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551681} {:answer/id #uuid "27d6879e-11ea-5047-b0de-3a3221a139a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=6{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551755} {:answer/id #uuid "ae976e85-aa05-5923-ae47-cc106ee58f91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:=6{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552086} {:answer/id #uuid "d050a82d-7b03-5d25-baca-61d6a9c6aedc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+6{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552159} {:answer/id #uuid "e51b6b71-81f0-5560-af0e-fb